      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Numpy for Machine Learning - Building a small Healthcare data to prepare it for machine learning."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RMiT5abzotPt"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Understanding features (X) and datasets (Y)\n",
        "Imagine a person may be at risk of a particular condition: Age, Cholestrol, Blood Pressure.\n",
        "\n",
        "These are our features presented by X\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HdnQJTzjpQ_W"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Example healthcare dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "Patient\t Age   \tBP  \tCholesterol\t  At risk(y)\n",
        "1\t       25\t   120\t      180\t        0\n",
        "2\t       40\t   135\t      210\t        1\n",
        "3\t       35\t   128\t      195\t        0\n",
        "4\t       55\t   145\t      240\t        1"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "_QfNS6lLqzqx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "X = np.array([\n",
        "              [25, 120, 180],\n",
        "              [40, 135, 210],\n",
        "              [35, 128, 195],\n",
        "              [55, 145, 240]\n",
        "])\n",
        "y = np.array([0,1,0,1])\n",
        "print(\"Feature:\", X)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Labels:\", y)\n",
        "print(X.shape)\n",
        "print(y.shape)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "Al4eBlw9qyRh",
        "outputId": "aa4345ae-5fba-4f98-a195-9033287f65a0"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Feature: [[ 25 120 180]\n",
            " [ 40 135 210]\n",
            " [ 35 128 195]\n",
            " [ 55 145 240]]\n",
            "Labels: [0 1 0 1]\n",
            "(4, 3)\n",
            "(4,)\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Why normalization matters - Some Machine learning algorithms may be affected by the difference in feature scale. We often therefore scale numerical features before training.\n",
        "\n",
        "Imagine two features\n",
        "1. Age: 25-55\n",
        "2. Cholestrol: 180-240"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AMfxuYpLulFb"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two Common Methods\n",
        "1. Min-Max Normalization\n",
        "   X_scaled = X - X_min/ X_max - X_min\n",
        "\n",
        "   The smallest value becomes 0 and the largest becomes 1.\n",
        "        "
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AT13HiT1x52L"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "values = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40, 50])\n",
        "normalized = (values - values.min())/(values.max()  - values.min())\n",
        "print(normalized)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "x0ElC_NE1oww",
        "outputId": "c2ee6f35-b3e3-4db9-8df6-8b159d5d56e6"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[0.   0.25 0.5  0.75 1.  ]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. Standardization (Z-score scaling): Instead of forcing values from 0 to 1 range, It transforms them so that each feature has.\n",
        "   Mean approximately 0\n",
        "   Standard deviation approximately 1\n",
        "\n",
        "   Z = (X - miu)/ sigma\n",
        "\n",
        "   X = orignal value\n",
        "   miu = mean\n",
        "   sigma = standard deviation"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "OLVLwZR61nCx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "values = np.array([10, 20, 30, 40, 50])\n",
        "mean = values.mean()\n",
        "std = values.std()\n",
        "\n",
        "Z = (values - mean)/std\n",
        "print(Z)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "jSTJa-pv2aL9",
        "outputId": "94bf0971-9140-4582-a43e-6fca6132efd6"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[-1.41421356 -0.70710678  0.          0.70710678  1.41421356]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A value of zero is exactly at the average. A positive values above the average and negative below the average."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7YY6XO4_BBXn"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Apply standardization to healthcare data set"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gtdHyLkhBSdx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "X = np.array([\n",
        "              [25, 120, 180],\n",
        "              [40, 135, 210],\n",
        "              [35, 128, 195],\n",
        "              [55, 145, 240]\n",
        "])\n",
        "X_mean = X.mean(axis=0)\n",
        "X_std = X.std(axis=0)\n",
        "X_standardization = (X - X_mean)/X_std\n",
        "print(X_standardization)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "fFPp3N-SB9Z6",
        "outputId": "a4a01428-4586-4cf7-a476-cef3328780d1"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": [
