          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[[-1.27017059 -1.3054279  -1.18321596]\n",
            " [ 0.11547005  0.32635698  0.16903085]\n",
            " [-0.34641016 -0.43514263 -0.50709255]\n",
            " [ 1.5011107   1.41421356  1.52127766]]\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Why axis=0?\n",
        "\n",
        "Because we want to calculate the mean and standard deviation separately for each feature (each column)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "aBzKpf_xDP_1"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Veryy very important********\n",
        "\n",
        "In real MAchine learning workflows, calculate the mean and the deviation using the training data only. and then use those values to transform the testing data.\n",
        "\n",
        "Otherwise information from the testing data may leak in to the training data. This is called data leakage"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "r1-Y7AlEDywj"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Splitting Data - Into traing and testing sets\n",
        "Training sets - Teaches model\n",
